Remember when Kate Middleton was basically a nobody? The British paparazzi enjoyed her "hotness" when she was dating Prince William, but she seemed an afterthought when she married Harry, which made her "fashionable without being a trend," as a Times reviewer put it at the time. But now the Duchess of Cambridge is a fashion icon. She's a trendsetter, a trendbreaker, and the role model for millions of younger British women. The numbers are there to prove it. The British public loves her. A recent poll found that the public is most positive about Meghan Markle. But when it comes to Kate, she's one of the most admired people in Britain. In a recent YouGov poll for the Sunday Times, Kate beat out a handful of other royals and popstars to land the title of the most admired person in the United Kingdom.
